1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,410
In the Universal Century, not every mobile suit gets to be the hero's machine.

2
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:23,440
R-X zero N, the Banshee Norn, Goddess of Fate:
the Earth Federation's second answer to the riddle of the Unicorn.

3
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,470
Like the Unicorn, she carries a psycho-frame,
armor that answers a Newtype's will.

4
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:46,180
When the N-T-D system awakens, the mask splits, the frame burns green,
and a machine of order starts to look disturbingly alive.

5
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,280
Her pilot is no chosen one. Riddhe Marcenas,
a Federation ace, fighting for duty rather than destiny.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,440
While Banagher rides the Unicorn toward answers,
Riddhe is ordered to silence them.

7
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:19,840
The two machines were built as sisters. In the dark of space
they do not simply fight: the Unicorn and the Banshee are pulling on each other.

8
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:28,540
And when the psycho-frame screams, it is not a curse. It was a prayer.

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,580
Near the end, sensors report resonance beyond every measurable limit,
as if countless hearts were sounding at once.

10
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,910
She was built to bury the secret of Laplace.

11
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:56,870
In the end, even the Federation's sharpest spear
could not stop the truth being born. We were blessed when we were born.

12
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:03,150
The Banshee Norn: the reluctant angel of the Universal Century.
